 - Latency: phase changes are pushed immediately. The big-screen stream coalesces only stats bursts (100ms), and a phase
   change cuts that pause short. (Before, every event waited 100ms.)
 
+## Question timer
+- Schema step 4: `quizzes.timer_minutes`, `quizzes.timer_seconds` ("Timer minutes" / "Timer seconds" on both quiz forms,
+  stored as typed so the form shows them back unchanged; 0..=999 / 0..=3599, blank = 0, missing = keep; 422 on error)
+  and `game_questions.time_limit` (seconds, copied from the quiz when the question opens, so editing the settings
+  mid-question doesn't change a running countdown). 0 = no timer. Not in the export format; imports get 0.
+- Deadline = `game_questions.opened_at + time_limit` (DB is the source of truth; reload or restart doesn't reset it).
+  `db::time_left_ms` gives the ms left; the big screen renders `[data-timer][data-left-ms]` (`role="timer"`, M:SS,
+  rounded up) in the open-question body only. Players never get it. The JS counts down from the *time left* (with
+  `performance.now()`), so the screen's clock doesn't matter.
+- Auto-finish: `game::run_timers` (spawned in `main`) checks `db::expired_games` every 100ms and runs the same
+  `db::advance(Finish, seq)` + `bump_phase()` as the "Finish" button. As a fallback, the screen JS POSTs `finish`
+  (with its `seq`, so it's a no-op if already done) 0.8s after reaching 0:00.
+- `db::save_answer` refuses answers once the time is up, even before the ticker has closed the question.
+
